{"records":[{"timestamp_text":null,"participants":["Bob Niran","ACC-B1"],"summary":"A service-desk ticket submitted using a contact name matching Bob Niran asked about access to the partially redacted account identifier. The ticket does not show authenticated access to ACC-B1 and cannot by itself establish ownership or control.","source_refs":[{"source_id":"b-support-001","source_locator":"case-b-scale/service-desk/ticket-44"}]},{"timestamp_text":null,"participants":["Bob Niran","ACC-B1"],"summary":"An email header displayed Bob Niran as the sender name in a discussion about account access, but lacked a verified account-control assertion, authentication context, and complete destination metadata. It supports only that Bob was mentioned in the correspondence, not that he controlled ACC-B1.","source_refs":[{"source_id":"b-email-001","source_locator":"case-b-scale/email/header-17"}]},{"timestamp_text":null,"participants":["Bob Niran","B-17","ACC-B1"],"summary":"The device inventory lists laptop B-17 as issued to Bob Niran, but no session record links the device to ACC-B1 and the inventory does not establish who used it during any relevant event. Device issuance is an association, not proof of account control.","source_refs":[{"source_id":"b-device-001","source_locator":"case-b-scale/device-inventory/laptop-B17"}]},{"timestamp_text":null,"participants":["Bob Niran","ACC-B1"],"summary":"An analyst note classifies the relationship between Bob Niran and ACC-B1 as not established. It identifies provider account records, login audit data, session identifiers, and authenticated device telemetry as needed for verification, and states that the classification is provisional and source-grounded.","source_refs":[{"source_id":"b-analyst-001","source_locator":"case-b-scale/analysis/control-status"}]}]}